.TH sys_fs 5 (date) "Linux man-pages (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
/sys/fs/ \- filesystems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /sys/fs/
.SH DESCRIPTION
This directory contains subdirectories for some filesystems.
A filesystem will have a subdirectory here only if it chose
to explicitly create the subdirectory.
.TP
.I /sys/fs/cgroup/
See
.BR sys_fs_cgroup (5).
.TP
.I /sys/fs/smackfs/
See
.BR sys_fs_smackfs (5).
.SH STANDARDS
Linux.
.SH HISTORY
Linux 2.6.0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sysfs (5)
